  "query_preview": "..\nThe leading edge of a sharp surface trough to the east is beginning \nto move into the Marianas coastal waters, with shower coverage to \nincrease considerably throughout the night, as well as thunderstorms \ndeveloping near midnight. Breezy conditions will ensue thereafter, \nwith on-and-off showers and some thunderstorms expected through at \nleast midweek, before improving in the second half of the week. As a \ndistant Tropical Depression Twelve (12W) passes the Marianas well to \nthe north-northeast, it will induce a more sustained monsoon flow \nacross the area coming into the weekend, so introduced higher PoP \ntrend toward the end of the forecast period.",
